<body style="height: auto; min-height: auto;">Hi ,<br />
<br />
It was good talking to you. &nbsp;I&#39;m sorry, that I had so many concerns but here is a list of options that you all could do to support the Red Cross -
<ol>
	<li>This is what we talked about on the phone. &nbsp;This would allow you to set up an online campaign and drive donors to existing sites.
	<ol>
		<li>https://sleevesup.redcrossblood.org</li>
	</ol>
	</li>
	<li>Outside of blood do donations&nbsp;we have serveral options
	<ol>
		<li>buying and packaging care kits for hospitals and military is pretty popular but there is cost. &nbsp;Minimum&nbsp;order is about $800.</li>
		<li>Sound the Alarm&nbsp;Campaign is a huge program
		<ol>
			<li>https://www.redcross.org/sound-the-alarm</li>
			<li>This is where we organize people to install fire alarms usual in low income area where the fire department secures as high fire risk neighborhoods. &nbsp;The installations happen on Saturdays but if an organization can&#39;t do Saturday they can also flier the neighborhood during the week so citizens know we&#39;re coming - this increases the number of people who let us in.</li>
		</ol>
		</li>
		<li>Organizing fundraisers</li>
	</ol>
	</li>
</ol>
These are the first four ideas that come to mind, but the options are not limited to these. &nbsp;<br />
<br />
Yours in Service,<br />
